= Planning & Controlling: Dynamic Operational Synergy

Planning and Controlling are inextricably linked, twin functions of management:
1. *Planning is Looking Ahead, Controlling is Looking Back:* Planning projects into the future, anticipating trends and setting targets. Controlling reviews past performance against those planned targets.
2. *Controlling is Blind Without Planning:* The controlling process begins with comparing actual performance against standards. If planning has not established measurable standards, controlling is impossible.
3. *Planning is Meaningless Without Controlling:* If actual performance is not monitored, measured, and corrected through controlling, plans remain mere academic exercises on paper.
